    "https://faculty.utexas.edu/career/190837": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Clinical Analytics, Research and Outcomes",
      "description": "Faculty Careers - The University of Texas at Austin UT Austin Home The University of Texas at Austin Faculty Careers All Positions Dell Medical School Executive Director of Clinical Analytics, Research and Outcomes Apply now Description The Director of Clinical Analytics, Research, and Outcomes will lead a multidisciplinary team that includes clinical research coordinators and quality and outcomes specialists. The Executive Director will oversee these efforts at Dell Children’s Medical Center and collaborate across a comprehensive healthcare platform that includes a broad range of services. The Executive Director will partner with clinical faculty to accomplish academic and care quality initiatives. These initiatives will expand research initiatives through collaborative engagements across hospital sections as well as other aligned stakeholders within the University of Texas at Austin and Ascension Texas hospitals. The primary goal of this position is to build sustainable, rigorous outcomes and research programs that advance the science and delivery of care for patients with congenital heart disease and their families. This will include establishing high‑quality clinical research, a robust data infrastructure, and a continuous quality measurement platform. The incumbent will be responsible for developing and maintaining data systems to measure key outcomes, leading prospective and retrospective studies, pursuing extramural funding, and partnering with clinical and quality teams to translate findings into practice. This position is a faculty‑level role at the Assistant Professor level or above, with active participation in the education and training of undergraduate, graduate, and medical students; residents; postdoctoral fellows; and other trainees, as well as participation in the academic activities of the Departments of Cardiovascular and Thoracic Surgery and Pediatrics. Key Responsibilities ·       Set and drive the strategic direction for a comprehensive outcomes and research program, including clinical research and data infrastructure for congenital heart disease care. ·       Recruit and mentor research colleagues in successful grant writing and acquisition and build a high-performing team. ·       Oversee the design and conduct of clinical research studies (prospective and retrospective) and clinical registries and databases, ensuring feasibility and alignment with program priorities. ·       Lead the development and implementation of data collection, data management, and analytics processes, including integration of clinical, administrative, and patient‑reported data sources. ·       Partner with quality and clinical operations teams to design, implement, and evaluate quality improvement initiatives that are informed by data and research findings. ·       Disseminate research and outcomes findings to internal and external audiences through reports, presentations, manuscripts, dashboards, visualizations, and other communication tools. ·       Train faculty, staff, and trainees in research methods, data interpretation, and best practices in outcomes and quality research. ·       Foster and create collaborations with Dell Medical School departments, UT Austin partners, and Ascension Texas to advise complex and strategic research and quality initiatives. ·       Oversee, prioritize, and activate research initiatives that lead to high-impact peer-reviewed publications, conference presentations, and extramural grant funding. Work with the Sponsored Programs Office on behalf of the researchers. ·       Ensure the quality of research work and data, drive research excellence, and maintain research team compliance with relevant regulations and best practices, including human subjects protections, data governance, and institutional policies. Qualifications Required Qualifications ·       Doctoral degree (MD, PhD, or foreign equivalent). ·       Demonstrated leadership or management experience. ·       Experience building and leading clinical research teams and operations, including oversight of data and/or quality improvement functions. ·       Strong knowledge of qualitative and quantitative research methodologies and their application. ·       Strong knowledge of biostatistics and research study design, data architecture, AI, and statistical programs (e.g., R, Python, STATA, SAS, etc.) ·       Strong knowledge of grant writing principles and best practices ·       Qualifications for faculty appointment at The University of Texas at Austin Dell Medical School at the level of Assistant Professor or above. Preferred Qualifications ·       MPH (Epidemiology, Biostatistics focus) or equivalent experience in epidemiological or outcomes research. ·       MBA, MHA, or equivalent experience in health care administration or management. ·       5+ years of formal leadership or management experience. ·       Clinical background and experience ·       Experience representing outcomes and clinical research with executive leadership and external partners. ·       Experience working on multiple fast‑paced research projects across the project lifecycle, from study design through dissemination. ·       Excellent communication skills, including the ability to translate complex data and research findings for diverse audiences. Application Instructions Interested and qualified candidates should complete the required application and submit a current CV. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement The University of Texas at Austin, as an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination and affirmative action. The University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all persons and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, disability, religion, or veteran status in employment, educational programs and activities, and admissions. College / School / Unit Dell Medical School Department Department of Cardiovascular Surgery Posted Aug 31, 2026 Apply by Open until filled Applying UT Austin uses Interfolio to manage the application process. Need help? Contact help and support . Share Email Facebook LinkedIn Twitter UT Austin Home Learn more about UT Contact us Phone 512-475-4363 Fax 512-475-7385 Email evpp-aps@utexas.edu 110 Inner Campus Dr. STOP G1000 Austin, TX 78712-1701 Careers Search Why UT Life & Work Quicklinks UT Austin Home Site Policies Web Privacy Policy Emergency Information Web Accessibility Policy Adobe Reader"
    },
    "https://faculty.utexas.edu/career/190768": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Integrative Shellfish Biology",
      "description": "Faculty Careers - The University of Texas at Austin UT Austin Home The University of Texas at Austin Faculty Careers All Positions College of Natural Sciences Assistant/Associate Professor in Integrative Shellfish Biology Apply now Description The Department of Marine Science and Marine Science Institute at The University of Texas at Austin (UTMSI) is seeking an assistant or associate professor in the field of Integrative Shellfish Biology. Fields of study can include, but are not limited to, physiology, functional biology, ecology and evolution, reproduction and development, disease, and host–pathogen interactions, as well as fisheries science and mariculture. We seek to fill this position in coordination with the development of a new state-of-the-art oyster mariculture research facility that will be located at the University of Texas Marine Science Institute’s Fisheries and Mariculture Laboratory in Port Aransas, Texas. In doing so, UTMSI is building the capacity to advance commercial oyster mariculture activities in the state of Texas, which includes facilities for broodstock husbandry, spawning, larval rearing, and spat production. As such, we are most interested in candidates that can make use of these facilities and contribute to the broader mission of the facility, but we strongly encourage applicants with both fundamental and applied research portfolios to apply. The Department of Marine Science is housed in the College of Natural Sciences and is home to an expanding group of 15 faculty who are engaging in research across a broad range of marine science disciplines. The successful applicant is expected to establish an internationally recognized, extramurally funded research program and mentor research personnel, teach at the graduate and undergraduate levels, and contribute to departmental service. The position is located at the University of Texas Marine Science Institute in Port Aransas, Texas, which is located 3.5 hours from Austin but holds strong collaborative ties to the research community on the university’s main campus, including the Department of Integrative Biology and the Jackson School of Geosciences. The Institute is home to the Department’s graduate degree program and has state-of-the-art laboratories and seawater-supplied facilities for experimental research. The Institute is also in close proximity to a variety of marine habitats that include near-pristine to anthropogenically altered estuarine ecosystems (oyster reefs, seagrasses, mangroves, saltmarshes, microbial mats, open water), with salinities ranging from oligohaline to hypersaline, as well as near- and offshore habitats of the Gulf of Mexico. The Institute hosts the Mission-Aransas National Estuarine Research Reserve, Beaufort Lagoon Ecosystems Long Term Ecological Research program, Fisheries and Mariculture Laboratory complex, and the Center for Coastal Ocean Science. The Institute also houses full-service core analytical facilities, a fleet of research vessels, and will take ownership of a new 78-ft All American Marine research vessel in spring 2027. This vessel will be fully equipped and specifically designed to support diverse research activities, including biological, geological, biogeochemical, and physical oceanography. Qualifications Required Qualifications Applicants must hold a PhD in marine science, biology, fisheries science, or a closely related field at the time of appointment. Postdoctoral or equivalent research experience is expected. Candidates must demonstrate the potential to establish (Assistant Professor) or an established record of (Associate Professor) an independent, externally funded research program in shellfish biology or a related discipline, along with a commitment to graduate and undergraduate teaching and mentorship. Appointment Rank The rank of appointment (Assistant or Associate Professor) will be commensurate with the candidate's experience and record. Appointment at the rank of Associate Professor requires a record of scholarly accomplishment, funding, and teaching sufficient to meet the University of Texas at Austin’s criteria for tenure. Application Instructions To apply Applicants should submit the following via Interfolio (ADD LINK): (i) a cover letter, (ii) a current CV, (iii) a research statement (up to 2 pages), (iv) a teaching, mentoring, and service statement (up to 2 pages), (v) contact information for three to five references (letters will be requested for top candidates), and (vi) three reprints of representative publications. Applications received prior to 15 October 2026 will receive full consideration. For additional information about the Institute and Department, see https://marinescience.utexas.edu and https://www.utmsi.utexas.edu. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement The University of Texas at Austin, as an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination and affirmative action. The University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all persons and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, disability, religion, or veteran status in employment, educational programs and activities, and admissions. College / School / Unit College of Natural Sciences Department Department of Marine Science Posted Aug 28, 2026 Apply by Open until filled Applying UT Austin uses Interfolio to manage the application process. Need help? Contact help and support . Share Email Facebook LinkedIn Twitter UT Austin Home Learn more about UT Contact us Phone 512-475-4363 Fax 512-475-7385 Email evpp-aps@utexas.edu 110 Inner Campus Dr. STOP G1000 Austin, TX 78712-1701 Careers Search Why UT Life & Work Quicklinks UT Austin Home Site Policies Web Privacy Policy Emergency Information Web Accessibility Policy Adobe Reader"
    },
    "https://faculty.utexas.edu/career/189936": {
      "title": "International Economic Policy (Assistant/Advanced Assistant Professor)",
      "description": "Faculty Careers - The University of Texas at Austin UT Austin Home The University of Texas at Austin Faculty Careers All Positions LBJ School of Public Affairs International Economic Policy (Assistant/Advanced Assistant Professor) Apply now Description The Lyndon B. Johnson School of Public Affairs at the University of Texas at Austin (“LBJ School”) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant or Advanced Assistant Professor of International Economic Policy to begin in Fall of academic year 2027-28 (with an August 2027 start date). One of the nation’s top programs in public affairs, the LBJ School is seeking to strengthen its faculty in international economics and trade. This faculty would support teaching in the Ph.D. in Public Policy, Master of National Security, Master of Global Policy Studies, and/or Bachelor of Arts and Master in Public Affairs. The appointee would teach courses on topics such as international economics and trade, international finance and monetary policy, development economics and industrial policy. Topics related to direct foreign investment, supply chain resilience, and commercial diplomacy would also be valued. Faculty research may focus on trade, geoeconomics, development economics, economic geography, international political economy, international macroeconomics and finance, labor economics of migration and remittances, global value chains and supply chain economics, foreign direct investment and multinationals, trade and climate, industrial policy. Candidates with prior applied policy research or related work experience will be viewed in a positive light in the search process.  The appointee will conduct and publish scholarly research and seek grant opportunities in support of their research and/or teaching activities. The appointee will participate in faculty governance at the LBJ School. Qualifications A Ph.D. in Economics, Finance, Political Economy, Political Science, or a related field is required. ABD candidates will be considered if the doctoral degree will be completed by the time of employment. Experience in college teaching and evidence of scholarship or scholarly potential is preferred. Application Instructions Interested candidates can submit their cover letter, CV, statement of teaching, three years of teaching evaluations (or fewer if unavailable), three letters of reference, and one article-length writing sample via Interfolio. Questions about the position can be directed to Andrew Waxman at awaxman@utexas.edu . Questions about the application can be directed to Shannon LaFevers at slafevers@austin.utexas.edu. The search committee will begin considering applications November 8, 2026 . The position will remain open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement The University of Texas at Austin, as an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination and affirmative action. The University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all persons and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, disability, religion, or veteran status in employment, educational programs and activities, and admissions. College / School / Unit LBJ School of Public Affairs Posted Aug 25, 2026 Apply by Open until filled Applying UT Austin uses Interfolio to manage the application process. Need help? Contact help and support . Share Email Facebook LinkedIn Twitter UT Austin Home Learn more about UT Contact us Phone 512-475-4363 Fax 512-475-7385 Email evpp-aps@utexas.edu 110 Inner Campus Dr. STOP G1000 Austin, TX 78712-1701 Careers Search Why UT Life & Work Quicklinks UT Austin Home Site Policies Web Privacy Policy Emergency Information Web Accessibility Policy Adobe Reader"
    },
